== Notes ==
*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
* The "ability to cast level 9 spells" may be better understood as the ability to learn level 9 spells (as [[wizard]]s are not required to know spells of the highest level they can cast).
*This feat can be selected by [[bard]]s. However, a bard cannot achieve the 9th level spell requirement on its own, so 17 levels of [[cleric]], [[druid]], or [[wizard]], or 18 levels of [[sorcerer]], would be needed.
*By removing the somatic [[component]] from spells, these feats eliminate the risk of arcane [[spell failure]] associated with wearing armor. Several arcane spellcaster builds acquire ''automatic still spell III'' along with one level in a warrior class that provides [[armor proficiency (heavy)|heavy armor]] and [[shield proficiency]]. This combination allows the spellcaster to gain up to 11 [[armor class|AC]] (8 from [[full plate]] and 3 from a [[tower shield]]), possibly plus a [[shield bonus]].
* Auto still spell does not add a metamagic icon to the spells it affects. The only indication that this feat is having an effect is the lack of spell failure due to armor and shield (and [[deaf]]ness, for some odd reason).

== Custom content notes ==
*A custom class must have this feat in their feat list, or that class will not be able to select it as a general feat.
